    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="1060" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg1048"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/11–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-30T20:00:00-05:00">November 30,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2431. Urtel 4009, November 29.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d799-f1"/> From Clayton.
                    Since preliminary discussions between Mr. Crowley and General Rudenko in which
                    General Rudenko requested a line of credit of $1 billion for purchase of
                    equipment in U.S. and which did not result in any commitment on part of this
                    Government, no further discussions have taken place.</p>
                <p>Dept has been pursuing policy of not encouraging active discussions and at
                    present matter is dormant. [Clayton.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d799-f1" n="22" xml:id="d799-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested information on “status of any negotiations of Soviet
                    Govt for Export-Import Bank credit.” (861.51/11–2945)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
